{
  "id": "benchmark-a",
  "title": "Requirement-heavy multi-stage approval workflow",
  "description": "Compound acceptance bullets, a multi-observation approval execution, a main and an alternative use-case flow, an operator duplicate-action risk, and an outage whose recovery the sources leave undefined.",
  "files": {
    "requirements.md": "# Approval workflow\n\n## RF-001 Submit a request\n\nAcceptance criteria:\n\n- Submitting a request creates a pending record and notifies the assigned approver.\n\n## RF-002 Approve a pending request\n\nAcceptance criteria:\n\n- Approving a pending request sets its state to Approved, records an audit entry,\n  and releases the reserved units.\n\n## RF-003 Reject a request without justification\n\nAcceptance criteria:\n\n- A request submitted without a justification is rejected and its state remains unchanged.\n\n## Use cases\n\nMain flow UC-1: the requester submits, the approver approves, the units are released.\nAlternative flow UC-1a: the approver returns the request for correction before approving.\n",
    "operations-manual.md": "# Operations manual\n\nSection SEC-1: open Requests, select New request, then Confirm.\nSection SEC-2: open Requests, select a pending request, then Approve.\nSection SEC-3: an approver who selects Approve twice on the same request sees the\nsecond attempt refused.\nSection SEC-4: when the ledger service is unavailable the approval screen reports a\ntransient failure. The manual does not state what happens to reserved units.\n"
  },
